This is a TEMPLATE only. It is not DKIM-signed, and it must not be sent as email.

To use it:

1. Run a removal example (for example python3 ../python/removal.py 192.0.2.1).
2. Copy the one-time token from ~/.iprx/<event_id>.token (mode 600). Never commit the token.
3. Replace TOKEN_FROM_POST_REMOVALS in the Subject (or mention the token in the body).
4. Send this message FROM an address at the PTR hostname's registrable domain, or the
   RDAP/WHOIS organisation or abuse-contact domain, using a mail server that adds a
   valid DKIM signature for that domain.
5. Save the delivered message as a raw .eml (including all headers) and upload it:

     ./10-dkim-upload.sh <event_id> message.eml

The upload scripts only POST a local file. They do not send email for you.
A failed DKIM check is recorded and stamped; the request does not advance until a check passes.
